if you're looking for an excuse to  return to The Witcher 3  it sounds like blood and wine might just  be it CD Projekt RED second and final  expansion takes place in the colorful  region of Tucson a Duchy untouched by  war southeast of tameria in the land of  anger 'n for those of us who skipped out  on oxenfurt geography class all you need  to know is that it's a new region  southeast of novigrad and it kind of  looks like a mediterranean countryside  this new region is roughly the size of  no man's land or novigrad and it's known  for its wine warm weather and wealth so  how you be spending time in Tucson well  the expansion adds 90 new quests a  hundred new pieces of armor some of  which include Witcher sets more than 30  new weapons a redesigned user interface  new mutations and a vineyard to relax in  gerelds name this should keep you busy  for around 20 to 30 hours oh and in case  you were interested there is a new  Skellig egwin deck if you don't have the  season pass you can get all this for 20  bucks when it launches but when does it  launch CD Projekt RED hadn't given an  exact date when they stopped by the  office but they sounded pretty confident  that it would drop either in May or June  from what I could tell during my  three-hour hands on preview blood and  wine takes place after the main story or  right before some of the final quests in  Wild Hunt just like hearts of stone if  you haven't finished the main game or if  you aren't a high enough level you will  have the option to start a new adventure  at the beginning of blood and wine can't  get used to the way you Knights talk  especially how you switch back and forth  between flowery and well there's  normally my first steps into salt  brought back memories of being washed  ashore and Skellig afore the first time  what's striking about this new region is  that you won't stumble across bloody  battlefields and people ready to take up  a side in the war in fact a lot of the  inhabitants seem to have their head in  the clouds ignoring what's really  happening in the continent and can you  blame them Toussaint's rolling green  hills colorful vegetation and warm skies  are a sight to see but it isn't just a  pretty picture dotted with more question  marks and exclamation points it felt  like a new world that's been around way  before it was created in the books or  when CD Projekt RED started designing it  the characters have a different accent  the armour and clothing looks nothing  like what I saw in temeria and the  landscape was entirely new in fact the  developer  that guided me through the preview said  many of the assets used in blood and  wine were created from scratch just like  the main game it's this detail that  pulled me right in you I do not know sir  nor seem you a knight yet still I'm  profoundly grateful nay indebted to you  for your succor  this trophy sir is yours but if this  setting caught my interest and it's the  characters that demanded it a year later  The Witcher threes engine still holds up  nicely but it's worth noting that I did  play this on PC the facial animations  are convincing the voice acting is as  good as you've come to expect and the  writing is still top-notch like hearts  of stone some of the best moments are  when Geralt felt like a fish out of  water for instance in one quest Geralt  must crash a festival in order to track  down a killer to find the killer he  needs to remove a ribbon from a horse  dress up his unicorn and find a golden  fish in a lake normally you'd have to  sneak up on the horse and actually fish  for the golden fish but time is of the  essence using signs in his Witcher  senses Geralt cheats his way to the end  I couldn't help but grin as girl  awkwardly tried to justify his behavior  to pissed off citizens blood and wine is  still dark and very gory but this  lighter tone lets the characters really  shine but talking and sunbathing isn't  all you'll be doing in blood and wine  you're still a Witcher and that means  you'll be slang plenty of monsters in  the three hours I played I fought four  bosses some were pretty standard sign  block parry attack but one in particular  forced me to change up my playstyle  simple blocks and attacks were useless  if you've played a Zelda game of two you  probably won't have much trouble  figuring out this bosses weaknesses but  the fight kept me on my toes and I was  excited to see what they threw at me  next  probably one of the biggest changes to  the combat are the new mutations this  adds another level to the progression  system a new mutagen skill tree lets you  unlock a dozen or so new skills perks  and abilities only one of these powerful  skills can be equipped at a time but  some appeared to have dramatic effects  one skill that I got to see was a  variation on art that increased its area  of effect and froze any enemies caught  in the blast these new skills could  allow for even more experimentation and  get even experienced players something  new and worthwhile to grind from what I  played at blood and wine seems like an  excellent send-off to a series I've  become so attached to but what about the  characters my favorite part of The  Witcher series has always been the  characters and I was a little  disappointed when I found out that ciri  Tris and yen did not play much of a role  in the last expansion I'm a little  worried that we may not see some of our  friends and allies that we've spent so  much time with but this is CD Projekt  RED we're talking about and letting down  their fans isn't something they  typically do  I can't wait to see who Geralt will meet  what he will fight and where this  adventure will take him
 

